## Style compared with the static Connection component

| | Static Connection component | Live demo edge (after P0-21) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Line | `.connection__line`: `stroke: var(--tone-d)`, `stroke-width: var(--border-width-strong)` | `.demo__edge-line`: `stroke: var(--tone-d)`, `stroke-width: var(--border-width-strong)` |
| Endpoint dots | `.connection__dot`: `fill: var(--tone-d)` | `.demo__edge-dot`: `fill: var(--tone-d)` |
| Width | 1.5 px (`--border-width-strong`) | 1.5 px (`--border-width-strong`) |
| Legend | `edge · --tone-d · 1.5 px` in `index.html` | same text next to the demo hint (`.demo__legend`) |

Before the change the demo line and dots used `--border-strong`; now both use the design-system
`--tone-d` connection style. No raw colour values and no new tokens were added
(`grep -nE '#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,8}|rgba?\(|hsla?\(' apps/web/preview/*` returns nothing).

## Demo stays permanent

`apps/web/preview/README.md` now states that the interactive demo stays permanently at the top of the
preview and that every change to the preview or to the design system updates the demo and refreshes
its screenshot in `reviews/evidence/` in the same task. The demo hint/legend also names the edge
style.

